se paper with a die-cut cover and gilded edges, this beautiful new Siglio edition allows readers to devour this crucial and compelling work.\nSophie Calle (born 1953) is an internationally renowned artist whose controversial works explore the tensions between the observed, the reported, the secret and the unsaid. She has mounted solo shows at major museums around the world and represented France at the Venice Biennale in 2007. Her most recent US exhibition was the acclaimed \"Rachel, Monique\" at the Episcopal Church of the Heavenly Rest in Manhattan in 2014.\nContent provided by Syndetic Solutions, Inc. Terms of Use\n... ( see more )\n\n    Subjects\n    Location\n    MARC\n    Full Record\n\nSubjects\nCalle, Sophie.\nArtists' books -- France.\nPhotography, Artistic.\n\nOther Author: \tBarash, Dany, translator.\nHatfield, Danny, translator.\nPenwarden, Charles, translator.\nLocation\nOnline\nLocation \tCall # \tStatus \tNotes\nArt Library \tTR654 .C323 2015 \tAvailable \t\nMARC\nLEADER 00000cam  2200445Ii 4500 \n001    898424858 \n003    OCoLC \n005    20160111090808.0 \n008    141219s2015    cauab         000 0 eng d \n020    1938221095 (hardback) \n020    9781938221095 (hardback) \n035    (OCoLC)898424858 \n040    YDXCP|beng|cYDXCP|dBTCTA|dOCLCQ|erda|dNYP|dCIA|dCDX|dOCLCF\n041 1  eng|hfre \n043    e-fr--- \n050  4 N7433.4.C266|bS8 2015 \n050  4 TR654|b.C323 2015 \n082 04 709.2|223 \n100 1  Calle, Sophie,|eauthor,|ephotographer. \n245 10 Suite vénitienne /|cSophie Calle ; translation, Dany \n       Barash, Danny Hatfield and Charles Penwarden. \n250    First edition. \n264  1 Los Angeles, California :|bSiglio,|c2015. \n300    1 volume (unpaged) :|billustrations, color maps ;|c21 cm \n336    text|btxt|2rdacontent \n337    unmediated|bn|2rdamedia \n338    volume|bnc|2rdacarrier \n500    \"Originally published in 1983 in French under the same \n       title by Éditions de l'Étoile, Paris. Published in English\n       in 1988 by Bay Press, Seattle, and in 1999 by Viol